From: Raven maintainers <74085717+Swamy-BV@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Recover retained identities with overlapping weak observations

A single missed detection moves an identity to Lost. Upstream excludes it from
the weak-observation pass, so continuing weak measurements cannot restore it.
Include retained lost tracks in that pass, using its stricter 0.5 IoU cost limit
and the existing reactivation branch. Class isolation, elapsed-time expiry and
strong new-track creation remain enforced by the adapter and preceding patch.
Only measurement-backed tracks are returned; no predicted boxes are published.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]
Signed-off-by: Raven maintainers <74085717+Swamy-BV@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/deploy/TensorRT/cpp/src/BYTETracker.cpp b/deploy/TensorRT/cpp/src/BYTETracker.cpp
--- a/deploy/TensorRT/cpp/src/BYTETracker.cpp
+++ b/deploy/TensorRT/cpp/src/BYTETracker.cpp
@@ -123,7 +123,10 @@
 	
 	for (int i = 0; i < u_track.size(); i++)
 	{
-		if (strack_pool[u_track[i]]->state == TrackState::Tracked)
+		// Retained identities may recover with measured weak boxes only under
+		// this pass's stricter IoU gate. Expiry is enforced before matching.
+		if (strack_pool[u_track[i]]->state == TrackState::Tracked ||
+			strack_pool[u_track[i]]->state == TrackState::Lost)
 		{
 			r_tracked_stracks.push_back(strack_pool[u_track[i]]);
 		}
